{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee, one of the vascular surgeons. You’re here today for a planned procedure on your transplanted kidney, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:22:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. They told me it’s called a coil embolization. I’m a bit nervous—what exactly does that mean?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:23:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. It’s a minimally invasive procedure where we block the blood flow to your failed transplant kidney using small metal coils. This helps avoid a major surgery to remove it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, so it’s not being taken out? I thought they might have to cut it out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:25:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. Because of your prior abdominal surgeries and mesh repair, removing it surgically could be risky. This is a safer option to let the kidney shrink over time without infection or pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:26:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. Will I feel anything during the procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:27:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be given sedation, so you’ll be very relaxed and won’t feel pain. We’ll go through a small puncture in your groin to reach the artery. It usually takes about an hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds better than open surgery. What about after? Will I be here long?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:29:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll need to stay flat in bed for a few hours to prevent bleeding at the site. Then, if all goes well, you could go home tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I do have a lot of medical history—kidney transplant, heart issues, thyroid—will that affect anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:31:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve reviewed your history. Your atrial fibrillation and thyroid condition are stable. We’ll continue your usual meds, except for a few adjustments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:32:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like what?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:33:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The transplant team recommended stopping Myfortic and starting a short course of steroids to help with inflammation. You’ll also keep taking tacrolimus as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:34:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ve been on Myfortic for years. Is it safe to stop?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:35:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, because the transplant kidney isn’t working anymore, we don’t need strong immunosuppression. The steroid taper will help your body adjust."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:36:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my warfarin? I’ve been off it since my last hospital stay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:37:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll restart it soon—your team plans for you to take 4 mg on Thursday, then follow up with your nephrologist for dosing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:38:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good, I was worried about my stroke risk with atrial fib."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2156-06-26 12:39:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re balancing bleeding and clotting risks carefully. Now, let’s get you prepped for the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2156-06-27 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You did well yesterday with the coil embolization. No complications, and the site looks clean."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2156-06-27 10:16:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I felt a little pressure but no pain. How long do I need to stay in bed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2156-06-27 10:17:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve already completed the 4-hour bed rest. You can sit up and walk now. We’ll monitor your blood pressure and the groin site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2156-06-27 10:18:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I walked a little earlier—felt fine. But my blood pressure drops after dialysis. I take midodrine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2156-06-27 10:19:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nephrology reviewed that. They’ll contact your nephrologist to adjust your midodrine if needed. For now, keep taking it as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2156-06-27 10:20:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I just get anxious when my BP drops too low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2156-06-27 10:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally understandable. We’ll keep an eye on it. You also had dialysis yesterday as scheduled?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2156-06-27 10:22:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, in the afternoon. I felt a bit weak afterward, but better by evening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2156-06-27 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. Your labs this morning are stable—creatinine is 4.4, which is expected since you’re on dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2156-06-27 10:24:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood count? I’ve been anemic before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2156-06-27 10:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hemoglobin is 9.6, a bit low but stable. No signs of bleeding. We’ll monitor it at your follow-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re preparing your discharge orders. You’re doing well—eating, walking, no pain or fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:31:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What meds am I going home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:32:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same as before, except Myfortic is stopped. You’ll take prednisone for six days—40 mg for three days, then 20 mg for three—then stop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:33:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, short course. And tacrolimus?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, three 0.5 mg capsules every 12 hours. Keep taking your other meds: amiodarone, levothyroxine, pravastatin, and valganciclovir twice a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:35:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And warfarin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:35:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take 4 mg on Thursday. Your INR will be checked soon after. Don’t miss that follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:36:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t. What about the incision? I don’t even have a big cut."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:37:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a small puncture. Keep it clean and dry. You can shower, but no baths or swimming until your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:38:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I have pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Acetaminophen for mild pain. Oxycodone if needed, but don’t drive while taking it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:40:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. When should I call the doctor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:41:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you develop fever over 101.5, severe pain, redness at the site, chest pain, or trouble breathing. Also, if you vomit and can’t keep fluids down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:42:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I’ll follow up with my nephrologist and transplant team?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:43:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’ll monitor your kidney function, INR, and adjust meds as needed. You’re doing well—this was a success."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I feel relieved this is done without major surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2156-06-27 12:45:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll discharge you in a couple of hours. Keep walking daily, no heavy lifting until your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2156-06-27 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. Your discharge papers are ready. You can go home now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2156-06-27 14:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again. I’ll follow all the instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2156-06-27 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call if anything changes. See you at your follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2156-06-26 12:21:00",
    "admission_end": "2156-06-27 16:50:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for a planned coil embolization of the renal artery to manage complications from a failed kidney transplant. Due to prior abdominal wall reconstruction, surgical removal was deemed high-risk, so a minimally invasive approach was chosen. The procedure was performed successfully without complications. Post-procedure, she remained on bedrest, ambulated without difficulty, and tolerated a regular diet. The transplant team recommended discontinuing Myfortic and initiating a short steroid taper, while continuing tacrolimus. She completed a scheduled hemodialysis session and had stable vital signs. Her warfarin was planned for restart post-discharge with INR monitoring. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions for incision care, activity, and follow-up with her nephrologist.",
    "problems": [
      "Complications of transplanted kidney",
      "Surgical operation with transplant of whole organ causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Aortocoronary bypass status"
    ]
  }
}
